---
// Schichtenbild von Matrix für „How Matrix was built“: wer die App benutzt, Adapter, gemeinsame Logik, Rust-Core, Modelle,
// Geräteverbund. Als HTML statt SVG, damit es auf dem Handy umbricht und lesbar bleibt. Inhalt belegt in ~/matrix/HANDBUCH.md §1.0
// und handbuch/peer.md; bei Architekturänderungen dort nachsehen.
---
<figure class="arch" aria-labelledby="arch-cap">
  <div class="layer">
    <span class="lbl">Who uses it</span>
    <div class="row four">
      <div class="box">iPhone and iPad</div>
      <div class="box">Mac and Windows</div>
      <div class="box">Browser<small>Linux container in your own network</small></div>
      <div class="box agent">Claude Code and other agents</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="layer">
    <span class="lbl">Adapters</span>
    <div class="row three">
      <div class="box">Tauri 2 app<small>React UI, typed calls into Rust</small></div>
      <div class="box">Web adapter<small>axum server, same calls over HTTP</small></div>
      <div class="box agent">MCP<small>inside the running app, or as a stand-alone program from npm</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mid">
    <div class="layer">
      <span class="lbl">Shared logic (Rust)</span>
      <div class="box wide">Import, ask with tools, tables, knowledge graph, background jobs, model pool</div>
      <span class="lbl">Core (Rust, no network, no UI)</span>
      <div class="box wide core">Chunking, embeddings, retrieval, SQLite<small>vectors as plain blobs, searched in pure Rust</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="layer side">
      <span class="lbl">Other Matrix devices</span>
      <div class="box">Paired over TLS in the local network<small>they lend their models, re-ranking and embedding</small></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="layer">
    <span class="lbl">Models, on the device by default</span>
    <div class="row four">
      <div class="box model">GGUF via llama.cpp<small>Metal, Vulkan or CPU</small></div>
      <div class="box model">ONNX Runtime<small>Core ML on Apple, CPU elsewhere</small></div>
      <div class="box model">Apple's on-device model</div>
      <div class="box model">whisper.cpp<small>speech to text</small></div>
    </div>
    <p class="opt">Optional: OpenAI-compatible endpoints, Azure, Ollama.</p>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="arch-cap">Everything above the core is a thin layer; the apps, the browser version and the agents call the same code.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .arch { margin: 0; display: grid; gap: 1.1rem; font-size: .95rem; }
  .layer { display: grid; gap: .45rem; }
  .lbl { font-weight: 700; font-size: .78rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .row { display: grid; gap: .55rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .row.four { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); } .row.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
  .row.three > :last-child:nth-child(odd) { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .row.three > :last-child:nth-child(odd) { grid-column: auto; } }
  .box { background: var(--bg); border: 1.5px solid var(--line-strong); border-radius: 10px; padding: .6rem .75rem; font-weight: 650; line-height: 1.3; }
  .box small { display: block; font-weight: 400; color: var(--muted); font-size: .84rem; margin-top: .2rem; }
  .box.agent { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .box.core { background: var(--fg); color: var(--bg); border-color: var(--fg); }
  .box.core small { color: var(--bg); opacity: .75; }
  .box.model { border-style: dashed; }
  .mid { display: grid; gap: 1.1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .mid { grid-template-columns: 2.2fr 1fr; align-items: start; } }
  .side .box { border-style: dotted; }
  .opt { margin: .1rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .88rem; }
  .arch figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
